# SYNC and SWITCH (EDIT again: the Banks page). Every track counts its place from one clock, so tracks of
# one length never part, whatever their lengths did meanwhile. SWITCH: a change of bank waits for the 1 of
# the phrase's next round of 1, 4 or 8 bars (the phrase's, not counted from the press). SYNC: from the
# change every track in line with track 1, which goes on where it is.
wait 200
expect bank 0
tap EDIT
tap EDIT
expect view 20
expect gpar32 1
expect gpar33 0
spin K2 2
expect gpar33 2
wait 50
shot banks.png
# Rnd len: on the Rhythm page (HOME twice), a %, 0 to start
tap HOME
tap HOME
expect view 1
expect tpar1 0
spin K3 25
expect tpar1 25
wait 50
shot rhythm.png
spin K3 -25
expect tpar1 0
# a copy is at once, whatever Switch says
tap SEL
tapkey w1
expect bank 1
tap PLAY
# bar 2 of the kick's two: the kick to 1 bar (it used to start its bar again here, off the hat)
wait 2600
tap HOME
expect view 0
expect track 0
spin K1 -1
expect tpar0 1
wait 400
expect aligned 1
# back to bank 1, in the phrase's 4-bar round: it waits for bar 5
tap SEL
tapkey w0
expect bank 1
expect bankwait 1
expect phrase <60
wait 4000
expect bank 1
expect phrase >50
expect phrase <64
wait 1500
expect bankwait 0
expect bank 0
expect phrase >63
expect phrase <76
expect aligned 1
expect last0 <16
# Now: at once again
tap EDIT
tap EDIT
spin K2 -2
expect gpar33 0
tap SEL
tapkey w1
expect bank 1
expect bankwait 0
wait 300
expect aligned 1
# stopped while one waits: it goes at once
spin K2 3
expect gpar33 3
tap SEL
tapkey w0
expect bankwait 1
tap PLAY
wait 50
expect playing 0
expect bankwait 0
expect bank 0
